.TH GTOP 1 "2026-11-08" "holyc" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gtop \- system monitor for the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gtop
[\fB\-f\fR \fISUBSTR\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-bpf\fR]
.br
.B gtop \-\-snapshot
[\fIW H\fR] [\fB\-\-keys\fR \fIKEYS\fR] [\fB\-f\fR \fISUBSTR\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A full\-screen monitor that reads
.I /proc
and
.I /sys
directly, with no libraries beyond libc. Panels: CPU (aggregate bar, trend graph, per\-core load, frequency, temperature),
RAM (used, zram, cache, swap and free as one segmented bar, trend graph), GPU (nvidia\-smi, else amdgpu sysfs, else
intel_gpu_top), TPU/NPU (shown only when the hardware exists), DISK (usage, activity and partition tree per device),
NET (rates, link speed and addresses per interface) and PROC.
.PP
PROC has two views, clean and raw, a process tree, marking, kill and a command palette.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-f " " \fISUBSTR\fR
keep only processes whose name contains SUBSTR
.TP
.B \-\-snapshot \fR[\fIW H\fR]
draw one frame as plain text and exit; needs no terminal. W and H set the size when both are given
.TP
.BI \-\-keys " KEYS"
feed keys before the snapshot is drawn: U D L R are the arrows, E is enter, any other character is literal.
A refresh happens after the keys, so a view change shows in the frame
.TP
.B \-\-no\-bpf
do not load the eBPF syscall counter. It loads only when run as root (or with CAP_BPF and CAP_PERFMON); otherwise the syscall column stays unknown
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
print usage
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B q
quit
.TP
.B Left, Right
switch the process view between clean and raw
.TP
.B Up, Down
move the cursor
.TP
.B Space
mark or unmark the process
.TP
.B k
send SIGKILL to the marked processes, or to the current row when none is marked
.TP
.B /
open the command palette
.TP
.B r
start or stop recording every number to
.I gtop\-record\-TIME.csv
in the current directory
.TP
.B a
anonymous mode
.TP
.B i
toggle the info display
.TP
.BR + ", " \-
refresh interval, 100 ms to 5 s in steps of 100 ms
.SH COMMAND PALETTE
Typing a name and its arguments after
.B /
runs the executable script
.IR commands/NAME ,
with the shell, passing the marked process ids as arguments. The name may not contain a slash or start with a dot. Its output is shown on the status line.
The scripts are looked up in
.IR $GTOP_COMMANDS ,
then
.IR ./commands ,
then next to the binary (\fIcommands\fR and \fI../share/gtop/commands\fR).
Shipped examples: \fBkill\fR, \fBterm\fR (SIGTERM), \fBsuspend\fR (SIGSTOP), \fBresume\fR (SIGCONT), \fBrenice\fR \fIN\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GTOP_COMMANDS
directory searched first for palette commands
.SH FILES
.TP
.I gtop\-record\-TIME.csv
written by the \fBr\fR key, TIME in seconds since the epoch
.TP
.I $PREFIX/share/gtop/commands/
the installed example commands
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 2 for an unknown option.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR top (1),
.BR proc (5)
